# Milestone M1 — Authentication & User Foundation

This plan implements secure Admin authentication, password hashing, JWT access & refresh token rotation, RBAC guards, and the frontend login interface according to `tradearena-prd.md` M1 scope.

## Scope & Components

### 1. Backend Authentication Module (`/backend`)
- **Dependencies**: `bcrypt`, `@types/bcrypt`, `@nestjs/jwt`, `@nestjs/passport`, `passport`, `passport-jwt`, `@types/passport-jwt`.
- **Database Layer**:
  - `PrismaService` & `PrismaModule` to interact with PostgreSQL models (`User`, `RefreshToken`).
  - Admin seed script (`prisma/seed.ts`).
- **Domain & Services**:
  - `UsersService`: User lookup, password verification, profile retrieval.
  - `AuthService`: Login, issue JWT access + hashed refresh tokens, token rotation on `/auth/refresh`, revocation on `/auth/logout`.
  - `JwtStrategy`: Passport JWT extraction from `Authorization: Bearer <token>`.
  - `JwtAuthGuard` & `RolesGuard`: Endpoint protection enforcing authentication and `Role.ADMIN`.
- **API Endpoints**:
  - `POST /api/v1/auth/login`: Authenticates admin email & password.
  - `POST /api/v1/auth/refresh`: Rotates refresh token and issues fresh access token.
  - `POST /api/v1/auth/logout`: Revokes refresh token.
  - `GET /api/v1/auth/me`: Protected endpoint returning authenticated user profile.
- **Automated Tests**:
  - `src/auth/auth.service.spec.ts`: Unit tests for login, credential validation, token rotation, and logout.
  - `test/auth.e2e-spec.ts`: E2E API tests covering valid login, invalid credentials (401), protected endpoint unauthorized access (401), and profile resolution (200).

### 2. Frontend Authentication & Shell (`/frontend`)
- **Login View (`/login`)**:
  - Responsive, dark-mode glassmorphic login card with validation and error states.
  - Integration with `POST /api/v1/auth/login`.
- **Auth State Management**:
  - Client-side auth context (`useAuth`) storing token and active user profile.
  - Auto-login check via `/api/v1/auth/me`.
- **Navbar & Navigation**:
  - Displays authenticated status, user badge, and Logout button.
  - Redirect logic to `/login` when unauthenticated.

